From 730e7511588d89dc1c0c02a2f715ac777985c84a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:29:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] G3 acceptance: the authoritative image boots to the kernel
 shell

COMPAT G3 (patch 0063).  The Stage-4 ELF parse FAILED boundary was root-caused
in the diagnostic bundle to SeaBIOS call32_post() reloading FS/GS with 64-KiB
real-mode limits before Stage 2's FAT copy.  The reviewed
stage2-fs-gs-restore.patch restores unreal mode on both disk-read exits and
preserves the caller frame with pushad/popad.

Acceptance build: the pinned AuraLite-OS source 518bef0 was rebuilt with the
release toolchain; a second worktree applied only that patch and reassembled
the same 6,656-byte Stage 2 (51ecc150...), byte-identical to the diagnostic
blob.  Both 81-MiB ISOs came from the release mkiso with ESP_MB=80 and differ
in exactly 10 of 166,272 sectors, all inside the Stage-2 staging area at LBA
34..46 (boot sector, GPT, FAT metadata, kernel, initrd and UEFI payload are
byte-identical).

Measured under the UNMODIFIED Debian SeaBIOS 1.16.3-2 bios.bin
(4ee65f3d...), --platform=haswell, AHCI ISO + blank USB, x86emu:
  pinned ISO     -> [BL4] ELF parse FAILED, halt in real16 (negative control)
  candidate ISO  -> ELF PT_LOAD segments copied, long mode,
                    [kernel] shell active; kmain idling., fault=0,
                    cap_reached=1
The candidate lane was run twice at cap=2,000,000,000; its serial stream and
stats block are byte-identical.  QEMU 10.0.13 with the same ROM reproduces the
split and additionally boots through ACPI RSDP found / ACPI MADT parsed.

Handoff: a temporary breakpoint at _start (0xffffffff80191640) records
rdi=0x10000 and BOOT_MAGIC at 0x10000; the 7,776-byte boot_info_t validates
against the generated offsets -- mmap_count=7 sorted E820 entries, HHDM
0xffff800000000000, initrd 0x1800000/0xb22000, cpu_count=1, bsp_lapic_id=0,
rsdp=0.

Gate: new test-g3 (54 checks over the SHA-256 manifest and completeness,
ordered serial receipts in both emulators, handoff layout/magic/E820/CPU/RSDP,
the deterministic Stage-2 blob and the replay) wired into make test; test-g3-nc
tampers five bundle copies and requires each to be rejected.  make test and
make test-sanitize are green.

Evidence: docs/evidence/compat-g3/acceptance/ (receipt, inputs, iso-layout,
commands, serial/stat captures, bootinfo.bin, SHA256SUMS).  The 2026-10-16
diagnostic bundle is marked as the root-cause trail.

Not established: no claim that the published d2110f8b... ISO itself boots --
kernel.elf embeds __DATE__/__TIME__, so bit identity is impossible; no
allocator-zone, CF9-causality or PERF P4 claim.  A separate measured blocker
is recorded for G5: with --lpc=ich9 the boot does not reach Stage 2 (at caps
300M and 1.5G instructions RIP sits at 0xefa1f inside SeaBIOS
ich9_lpc_setup with repeated PCI enumeration); cause not established, and
G4's table-publication receipts are unaffected.
